{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function queue<TValue>(fn, initialOptions): (item, position, runOnItemsChange) => boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/queuer.ts#L745","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queuer.ts:745"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a queue that processes items immediately upon addition.\nItems are processed sequentially in FIFO order by default."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to asyncQueue when you need promises, retry support, abort capabilities, concurrent execution, or advanced error handling."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses TanStack Store for reactive state management"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" to provide initial state values when creating the queuer"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onExecute"},{"type":"text","value":" callback to react to item execution and implement custom logic"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onItemsChange"},{"type":"text","value":" callback to react to items being added or removed from the queue"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onExpire"},{"type":"text","value":" callback to react to items expiring and implement custom logic"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onReject"},{"type":"text","value":" callback to react to items being rejected when the queue is full"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The state includes execution count, expiration count, rejection count, and isRunning status"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State can be accessed via the underlying Queuer instance's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"store.state"},{"type":"text","value":" property"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using framework adapters (React/Solid), state is accessed from the hook's state property"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example usage:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Basic sequential processing\nconst processItems = queue<number>((n) => console.log(n), {\n  wait: 1000,\n  onItemsChange: (queuer) => console.log(queuer.peekAllItems())\n});\nprocessItems(1); // Logs: 1\nprocessItems(2); // Logs: 2 after 1 completes\n\n// Priority queue\nconst processPriority = queue<number>((n) => console.log(n), {\n  getPriority: n => n // Higher numbers processed first\n});\nprocessPriority(1);\nprocessPriority(3); // Processed before 1","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"item"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"initialoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"initialOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/QueuerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueuerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"code","value":"(\n   item,\n   position?,\n   runOnItemsChange?): boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adds an item to the queue. If the queue is full, the item is rejected and onReject is called.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot be queued (it is the internal \"no item\" sentinel) and is always rejected.\nItems can be inserted based on priority or at the front/back depending on configuration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns true if the item was added, false if the queue is full."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example usage:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"queuer.addItem('task');\nqueuer.addItem('task2', 'front');","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"item","children":[{"type":"text","value":"item"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"position","children":[{"type":"text","value":"position?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/QueuePosition.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueuePosition"}]},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"..."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"runonitemschange","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runOnItemsChange?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"initialoptions","text":"initialOptions","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"item","text":"item","level":4},{"id":"position","text":"position?","level":4},{"id":"runonitemschange","text":"runOnItemsChange?","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction queue<TValue>(fn, initialOptions): (item, position, runOnItemsChange) => boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [queuer.ts:745](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/queuer.ts#L745)\n\nCreates a queue that processes items immediately upon addition.\nItems are processed sequentially in FIFO order by default.\n\nThis synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to asyncQueue when you need promises, retry support, abort capabilities, concurrent execution, or advanced error handling.\n\nState Management:\n- Uses TanStack Store for reactive state management\n- Use `initialState` to provide initial state values when creating the queuer\n- Use `onExecute` callback to react to item execution and implement custom logic\n- Use `onItemsChange` callback to react to items being added or removed from the queue\n- Use `onExpire` callback to react to items expiring and implement custom logic\n- Use `onReject` callback to react to items being rejected when the queue is full\n- The state includes execution count, expiration count, rejection count, and isRunning status\n- State can be accessed via the underlying Queuer instance's `store.state` property\n- When using framework adapters (React/Solid), state is accessed from the hook's state property\n\nExample usage:\n```ts\n// Basic sequential processing\nconst processItems = queue<number>((n) => console.log(n), {\n  wait: 1000,\n  onItemsChange: (queuer) => console.log(queuer.peekAllItems())\n});\nprocessItems(1); // Logs: 1\nprocessItems(2); // Logs: 2 after 1 completes\n\n// Priority queue\nconst processPriority = queue<number>((n) => console.log(n), {\n  getPriority: n => n // Higher numbers processed first\n});\nprocessPriority(1);\nprocessPriority(3); // Processed before 1\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`item`) => `void`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`QueuerOptions`](../interfaces/QueuerOptions.md)\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n```ts\n(\n   item,\n   position?,\n   runOnItemsChange?): boolean;\n```\n\nAdds an item to the queue. If the queue is full, the item is rejected and onReject is called.\n`undefined` cannot be queued (it is the internal \"no item\" sentinel) and is always rejected.\nItems can be inserted based on priority or at the front/back depending on configuration.\n\nReturns true if the item was added, false if the queue is full.\n\nExample usage:\n```ts\nqueuer.addItem('task');\nqueuer.addItem('task2', 'front');\n```\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### item\n\n`TValue`\n\n#### position?\n\n[`QueuePosition`](../type-aliases/QueuePosition.md) = `...`\n\n#### runOnItemsChange?\n\n`boolean` = `true`\n\n### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: queue\ntitle: queue\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction queue<TValue>(fn, initialOptions): (item, position, runOnItemsChange) => boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [queuer.ts:745](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/queuer.ts#L745)\n\nCreates a queue that processes items immediately upon addition.\nItems are processed sequentially in FIFO order by default.\n\nThis synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to asyncQueue when you need promises, retry support, abort capabilities, concurrent execution, or advanced error handling.\n\nState Management:\n- Uses TanStack Store for reactive state management\n- Use `initialState` to provide initial state values when creating the queuer\n- Use `onExecute` callback to react to item execution and implement custom logic\n- Use `onItemsChange` callback to react to items being added or removed from the queue\n- Use `onExpire` callback to react to items expiring and implement custom logic\n- Use `onReject` callback to react to items being rejected when the queue is full\n- The state includes execution count, expiration count, rejection count, and isRunning status\n- State can be accessed via the underlying Queuer instance's `store.state` property\n- When using framework adapters (React/Solid), state is accessed from the hook's state property\n\nExample usage:\n```ts\n// Basic sequential processing\nconst processItems = queue<number>((n) => console.log(n), {\n  wait: 1000,\n  onItemsChange: (queuer) => console.log(queuer.peekAllItems())\n});\nprocessItems(1); // Logs: 1\nprocessItems(2); // Logs: 2 after 1 completes\n\n// Priority queue\nconst processPriority = queue<number>((n) => console.log(n), {\n  getPriority: n => n // Higher numbers processed first\n});\nprocessPriority(1);\nprocessPriority(3); // Processed before 1\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`item`) => `void`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`QueuerOptions`](../interfaces/QueuerOptions.md)\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n```ts\n(\n   item,\n   position?,\n   runOnItemsChange?): boolean;\n```\n\nAdds an item to the queue. If the queue is full, the item is rejected and onReject is called.\n`undefined` cannot be queued (it is the internal \"no item\" sentinel) and is always rejected.\nItems can be inserted based on priority or at the front/back depending on configuration.\n\nReturns true if the item was added, false if the queue is full.\n\nExample usage:\n```ts\nqueuer.addItem('task');\nqueuer.addItem('task2', 'front');\n```\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### item\n\n`TValue`\n\n#### position?\n\n[`QueuePosition`](../type-aliases/QueuePosition.md) = `...`\n\n#### runOnItemsChange?\n\n`boolean` = `true`\n\n### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n"}
